Suppose for contradiction that for all choices of constants $c_1$ and $C_2$, there exist parameters $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ such that $A_L(\tau_1,\tau_2) < c_1 \min(\tau_1, \tau_2^{C_2})$, i.e. there exists a map $\alpha \in (\mathbb{R}^m)^*$ and a map $\varphi \in (\mathbb{Z}^d)^T$ such that  $\tau_1\leqslant \Vert \alpha\Vert_\infty \leqslant \tau_2^{-1}$ and 
\begin{equation}
\label{first of lemma alg coeffs}
